The user refined two multiple-choice questions regarding the limitations of standard panel regressions and cross-sectional climate-impact studies in the context of climate change research. For the question on panel regressions, they aimed to clarify that such methods struggle with external validity because they utilize temporary, localized, and unanticipated weather shocks, making it difficult to capture the widespread and persistent nature of climate change. For the question on cross-sectional studies, the user sought to emphasize the risk of omitted-variable bias where unaccounted factors might influence differences across locations, creating misleading conclusions about the effects of climate. Both questions were adjusted to make correct answers less obvious.
